  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Environment Africa - Livelihoods Protection and Promotion Zimbabwe</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Approximately 35000 of the rural and urban poor and most vulnerable households (approximately 15,000 people) are having their livelihoods sustained through a combination of interventions including facilitation of environmental education and training, provision of agricultural resources, provision of agriucltural extension and training services,provision of alternative efficient and cleaner energy options, waste management and mitigation of the impact of HIV &amp; AIDS (OVC support, ISALS, IGAs, School Block Grants) and climate change.</narrative>
  </description>
